    "changelog": "## What's New in v6.3.5\n\n### Fixed\n- AED no longer stops with a silent \"exited 1\" on some machines. Its watchdog killed healthy jobs whenever Windows would not let it check on the app; it now exits only when the app is really gone.\n- After AED, the app no longer starts an extra background clustering job per recording. It slowed bulk runs and removed waste-pool entries that clustering had just saved.\n- Dawn/day/dusk/night tags are worked out from the time of day without starting Python.\n- Includes 6.3.4: Perch embedding clustering runs Perch once per event.",
